### Problem description

Something in `T.copy` seems to completely break when copying to what I believe is shared memory when `coalesced_width` is unset in the kwargs.

The main difference is that this fails (somehow):
```c
*(threadgroup bfloat*)(shared + (((int)threadIdx.x) * 4)) = src[((((int)threadIdx.x) * 4) / 4)];
threadgroup_barrier(mem_flags::mem_threadgroup);
```
and this works correctly:
```c
for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
  shared[((i * 128) + ((int)threadIdx.x))] = src[((i * 128) + ((int)threadIdx.x))];
}
```

I'm not a low-level kernel developer so I have absolutely no idea what the practical difference is! :p 

